WEBVTT

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:10.108
Now, a miracle is about
to be created upon this planet.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.183
Did you sleep well?

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.263
So where are we now?

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.700
We just left Ashiya, so we should
get into Sannomiya soon.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.826
Yeah?

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.474
Sorry for making you
leave your bike.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.742
It's all right.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.677
I'll get my dad to
buy me a new one.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.946
Hey. That's not right.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:50.083
The break in the oil
is the break in the bonds.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:53.019
All bonds will eventually break.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.611
That's how...

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.280
"That's how everything revolves."

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:02.995
Hey, hey.

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:08.034
That old man on the mountain
get to you?

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.023
Huh?

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.838
Come to think of it...

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:15.069
...we were with him for four days,
but we didn't even get his name.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:21.512
"A name shall have nothing
to do with how things stand."

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.014
I think the old man
got to you, too.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:34.149
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:40.496
Episode 5: The Small Voices

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.545
What's that smell?

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.035
How is the city?

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.875
Can you bear the way
you are now?

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.656
What's that Chris
snooping around for?

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:04.884
Let's go.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.694
Where're you going, Tokio?

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.529
Can't go home yet.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:12.464
I haven't been in touch with home
for almost a week, you know.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.464
Juna?

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:24.074
I knew it was Juna!
And Tokio, too!

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.775
Sayuri?

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.686
Commander Onizuka.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.383
It's you.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:16.763
This must be water from Okusaga.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:19.632
Don't you think water containing
chlorine and nitrogen oxide...

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.032
...would be too inelegant?

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:28.141
About the information
on that infectious disease...

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.109
...which causes total paralysis.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:35.103
Apparently, the Australian Branch
of S. E. E. D. Leaked it intentionally.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:40.079
Do you think it's related to
genetically modified foods?

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:43.823
It appears to be a new type
of virulent intestinal bacteria...

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.658
...similar to the Botulinus toxin.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.182
Nothing else is known.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:50.763
Already in Kobe, Osaka
and Gifu...

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:54.563
...there have been outbreaks in
various cities in western Japan.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:59.038
That TI-2 girl...

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.903
Juna, was it?

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.109
Can we use her?

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:05.771
She hasn't completely
awakened yet.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:08.245
I see.

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:19.118
That means we can only
count on Chris, the TIl-1.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:33.295
Look, if you don't eat, we'll have
to hook you up to the IV.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.504
Please, Chris.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.339
What's so funny?

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.180
Well...

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:45.241
...there's another one who's
having difficulty eating.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.944
Here goes!

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:54.259
I swear I dreamed of this taste.

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.330
You going to eat that?

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.024
Huh?

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:02.167
I was thinking about something
the old man was saying.

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.597
That this is going
to become a part of me.

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.170
No, no...

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.076
If you start thinking like that...

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:12.135
...you won't be able
to eat anything in the city.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.884
Sorry. I got tied up with something.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:20.148
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:22.218
There.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:25.224
You found something cool.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.919
Where'd you find it? Moto-Koh?

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.996
Oh! Th-This?

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.429
Well...

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:34.100
Hey, what happened
to your glasses?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.668
Look a little different, huh?

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:39.035
I have to buy another pair
because I need a new prescription.

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:42.308
You look better without glasses.

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.142
You think?!

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.811
I'm happy even if that's a lie!

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:47.279
It's true! It's true! It's great!

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:57.420
What is this?

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:07.026
What is this?!

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:12.105
Mr. Tanabe, the vice principal,
asked me about you.

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:15.174
But I said it's between you guys,
after all...

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.909
Oh, don't worry.

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:19.400
I didn't tell him anything weird.

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:24.517
So it's become a rumor, huh?

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.753
That's not really true.

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:28.988
But where did you two go,
anyway?

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:31.023
Just a little trip.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.650
To help work in the fields.

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:35.854
Yeah, right!

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:40.233
I can't imagine you
doing any physical labor.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:42.428
You're some rich boy
from Tokyo, after all.

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:46.038
- Is it true?
- It's true.

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:47.699
- I swear it's true.
- Liar.

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:50.871
- Liar.
- It's a lie.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.648
How is the city?

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:58.947
Can you bear the way
you are now?

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:03.156
I got my hands all dirty
and I worked hard.

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:06.092
Yeah, yeah.
I'll go along with your story.

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:07.226
Oh, right!

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:10.329
The goodwill match against
3rd High was amazing!

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:12.432
That girl who came in second
at the Inter High games...

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:15.101
...you should've seen her archery.

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:18.304
It's like she casts her soul
onto the target.

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:19.439
Even coach was saying that...

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:23.637
...that's the kind of talent
you see only once in 20 years.

00:07:24.076 --> 00:07:25.338
Juna?

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:27.537
Juna?

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:29.378
What's the matter?

00:07:29.816 --> 00:07:32.418
Juna. Hey, Juna?

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.420
Hey, are you not feeling well?

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:35.455
What's the matter?

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:36.945
You all right?

00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:46.261
Hang on a second.

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:49.368
What are you sulking about?

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:50.733
I'm not sulking.

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:52.602
Yeah, but...

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:57.710
What could I have done?

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:01.612
People would've thought you were
in mourning or something.

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:02.937
So...

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:07.283
I don't really understand
you anymore.

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:10.556
Here I thought you ran away
and eloped with Tokio...

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:14.549
...but you two are just an awkward
couple who haven't even kissed.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:21.934
I just want you two to get along.
You understand?

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.458
You too, Oshima.

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:28.306
The pavement
feels like it's moving...

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:30.776
Oshima?!

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:31.674
Tokio!

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:36.443
Mom! Mom! Open the door!

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.343
Juna?

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:39.848
Is that Juna?

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:46.158
Juna! Where have you been?
I've been worried sick!

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:47.560
I'm sorry, Mom.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.795
Could you please
call an ambulance?!

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:51.854
Oshima's very sick!

00:08:53.099 --> 00:08:56.035
Yes. That's right.

00:08:56.035 --> 00:08:58.060
The name is Ariyoshi.

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:00.996
Yes, please hurry up.

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:04.644
So, rather than simply vomiting,
he's having convulsions...

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:07.613
...and his respiration
is also unsteady?

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:10.983
That's right.
He's suffering so much.

00:09:10.983 --> 00:09:12.285
I understand.

00:09:12.285 --> 00:09:14.753
I'll be sending an ambulance
there right away.

00:09:15.054 --> 00:09:17.249
And do as the
ambulance medics tell you.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.798
Don't worry, Tokio.

00:09:25.798 --> 00:09:27.700
The ambulance will be here
right away.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.802
Oshima! Drink this!

00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:31.170
Come on. Open up.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.728
Open your mouth!

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:37.810
Now, just take it easy.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.107
Just take it easy.

00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:40.341
Right.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.592
What's the matter?

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:54.059
You just took the medicine!

00:09:56.162 --> 00:09:57.220
Tokio!

00:09:57.663 --> 00:09:58.493
Tokio.

00:10:05.371 --> 00:10:06.338
What?!

00:10:08.207 --> 00:10:09.071
Juna!

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:15.477
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:10:16.215 --> 00:10:18.351
Kaine, where are you right now?

00:10:18.351 --> 00:10:21.684
Kaine!
Your sister's in trouble!

00:10:22.054 --> 00:10:24.824
Huh? You're going for
a drive with your friends?

00:10:24.824 --> 00:10:26.726
What are you talking about?

00:10:26.726 --> 00:10:30.062
- Juna's your sister!
- Does he really have to be isolated?

00:10:30.062 --> 00:10:30.863
Now, come on!

00:10:30.863 --> 00:10:33.099
- We must prevent it from spreading.
- Just come here!

00:10:33.099 --> 00:10:34.828
We must take
emergency precautions.

00:10:39.438 --> 00:10:42.066
TI-2.
Confirming bio field reaction.

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:44.877
Bio field sensor calibrated.

00:10:44.877 --> 00:10:45.911
TI-2 response.

00:10:45.911 --> 00:10:49.882
Traveling from the duodenum
to the small intestine.

00:10:49.882 --> 00:10:53.853
Until we can determine
the toxic substance or virus...

00:10:53.853 --> 00:10:56.549
...do not administer
any antibiotics to the boy.

00:10:56.956 --> 00:10:58.824
If there is any resistance
to the medicine...

00:10:58.824 --> 00:11:00.883
...we won't be able to deal with it.

00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:05.765
Oops. Big trouble.

00:11:05.765 --> 00:11:10.302
There's a micro Raaja response
within the body of TI-2, too.

00:11:10.302 --> 00:11:13.897
The Raaja's spread to Juna,
I mean, to TI-2 as well?!

00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:17.076
If it gets worse and
she were to die for us...

00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:20.046
...we'll have a chance to track
down where the TI Spirit Body...

00:11:20.046 --> 00:11:22.105
...will end up after the body dies.

00:11:23.849 --> 00:11:26.215
TI-2 has arrived in the
patient's large intestine.

00:11:33.225 --> 00:11:34.522
What?

00:11:35.928 --> 00:11:40.194
Don't tell me I'm in Tokio's body!

00:11:42.234 --> 00:11:44.603
The beneficial bifidobacteria
and enterococcus...

00:11:44.603 --> 00:11:46.305
...and the bad clostridium
perfringens and E. Coli...

00:11:46.305 --> 00:11:49.375
...all of the growth in
bacterial flora has fallen.

00:11:49.375 --> 00:11:53.212
His immunity has decreased
to about 10 percent of normal.

00:11:53.212 --> 00:11:56.382
Because his normal intestinal
bacteria has been weakened...

00:11:56.382 --> 00:11:59.408
...it must have allowed in
the Bacterio Raaja.

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:02.783
Lymph has been secreted from
the walls of the large intestine.

00:12:21.807 --> 00:12:23.409
Bacterio Raaja from the bacteria...

00:12:23.409 --> 00:12:24.944
...and the lymph secretion.

00:12:24.944 --> 00:12:27.003
It's causing a disturbance
in the intestine.

00:12:42.161 --> 00:12:44.363
Raaja response has
spread to the rectum.

00:12:44.363 --> 00:12:46.232
Patient's respiratory capability
now affected.

00:12:46.232 --> 00:12:47.563
He can't take much more.

00:12:48.467 --> 00:12:49.468
Medical section.

00:12:49.468 --> 00:12:50.836
Administer antibiotics
to the patient.

00:12:50.836 --> 00:12:51.962
No use!

00:12:52.171 --> 00:12:55.441
After analysis of
the patient's lymph gland...

00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:58.110
...there're an analgesic drug,
insecticide...

00:12:58.110 --> 00:12:59.612
...preservative compounds...

00:12:59.612 --> 00:13:02.348
...and there's also livestock
growth hormones.

00:13:02.348 --> 00:13:03.115
And...

00:13:03.115 --> 00:13:05.606
Antibodies used in meat...

00:13:06.452 --> 00:13:10.912
Chemicals or food additives
seem to be having a negative effect.

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:14.088
It's getting him from all sides!

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.428
Damn you!

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:26.135
You fool.

00:13:26.906 --> 00:13:27.940
No, Chris.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:30.465
You'll die if you
go in such a weak state!

00:13:37.183 --> 00:13:40.719
There's another TI Spirit Body
response in addition to the TI-2.

00:13:40.719 --> 00:13:41.743
It's Chris.

00:13:42.388 --> 00:13:44.015
Why do you fight?

00:13:44.523 --> 00:13:45.624
Chris!

00:13:45.624 --> 00:13:48.561
Why?! The Raaja's here!

00:13:48.561 --> 00:13:50.620
If I don't fight it,
Tokio's going to die!

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:53.933
What did you learn
up in the mountain?

00:13:53.933 --> 00:13:54.763
What?

00:13:55.167 --> 00:13:57.635
What does this have to
do with the mountain?!

00:13:58.904 --> 00:14:01.498
You must sense its true form.

00:14:02.007 --> 00:14:03.565
On your own.

00:14:06.312 --> 00:14:07.210
Huh?

00:14:07.546 --> 00:14:08.513
Let's go.

00:14:19.258 --> 00:14:23.888
TI-1 and TI-2 responses have
moved to the body of TI-2.

00:14:24.663 --> 00:14:25.721
What?!

00:14:26.265 --> 00:14:30.002
You don't seem to know anything
about what's in your own body.

00:14:30.002 --> 00:14:33.172
What? We're in my stomach?

00:14:33.172 --> 00:14:35.003
It's gross.

00:14:35.808 --> 00:14:39.335
Is it dirty? Is it gross?

00:14:39.612 --> 00:14:43.514
Can you not even accept
your own body?

00:14:43.916 --> 00:14:45.850
Even your own body...

00:14:46.752 --> 00:14:48.320
Try to remember.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.551
The mountain showed
its true face to you.

00:14:51.657 --> 00:14:53.259
How about those fields?

00:14:53.259 --> 00:14:55.284
Mountain? Fields?

00:14:55.494 --> 00:14:57.196
Try to remember.

00:14:57.196 --> 00:14:59.031
The sacred mountain...

00:14:59.031 --> 00:15:02.523
...and the fields brimming with
the life of insects and grasses.

00:15:03.068 --> 00:15:07.027
The true nature of
all those tiny life forms.

00:15:13.545 --> 00:15:17.283
The insects and weeds...

00:15:17.283 --> 00:15:19.683
...are not the enemy.

00:15:20.252 --> 00:15:23.483
They all have roles to play.

00:15:24.757 --> 00:15:28.284
Is the stomach the same
as the land?

00:15:30.963 --> 00:15:33.499
That TI-2 girl is pretty impressive.

00:15:33.499 --> 00:15:37.036
The amount of intestinal bacteria
she has is no small quantity.

00:15:37.036 --> 00:15:38.737
Her experience on the mountain...

00:15:38.737 --> 00:15:41.407
...must have increased the
amount of bacteria in her body...

00:15:41.407 --> 00:15:44.376
...which had the effect of
suppressing the Raaja in her.

00:15:44.376 --> 00:15:45.468
- It's coming.
- Huh?

00:15:49.615 --> 00:15:50.749
The Raaja?!

00:15:50.749 --> 00:15:52.051
That's right.

00:15:52.051 --> 00:15:53.985
It's spread to you as well.

00:15:54.186 --> 00:15:55.778
Me, too?

00:15:56.822 --> 00:15:59.425
It's my own body...

00:15:59.425 --> 00:16:01.416
...but I didn't even realize it.

00:16:01.927 --> 00:16:03.262
And so...

00:16:03.262 --> 00:16:05.560
...what do you intend on doing?

00:16:06.031 --> 00:16:07.896
What are you going to do?

00:16:13.939 --> 00:16:15.741
Two more victims of the
infection in the Tohoku area.

00:16:15.741 --> 00:16:17.943
We've stopped the water supply...

00:16:17.943 --> 00:16:18.807
What now...?

00:16:23.882 --> 00:16:25.217
Mrs. Ariyoshi?

00:16:25.217 --> 00:16:27.186
She finally came home, after all.

00:16:27.186 --> 00:16:30.489
I thought I'd make her
her favorite kushikatsu.

00:16:30.489 --> 00:16:31.957
What do you mean?

00:16:31.957 --> 00:16:34.026
You must be hungry, too.

00:16:34.026 --> 00:16:36.324
You've got to get a hold of yourself.

00:16:37.896 --> 00:16:40.091
If something were to
happen to that girl...

00:16:40.532 --> 00:16:44.127
...what am I going to say to her
dearly departed grandmother?

00:16:45.571 --> 00:16:48.474
My grandmother once
told me that...

00:16:48.474 --> 00:16:50.609
...when you're really ill...

00:16:50.609 --> 00:16:52.311
...drink a potion made from
your umbilical cord.

00:16:52.311 --> 00:16:53.278
HQ!

00:16:53.278 --> 00:16:54.142
I heard that.

00:16:54.446 --> 00:16:55.447
Well? What do you think?

00:16:55.447 --> 00:16:57.210
I'm doing it.

00:16:58.617 --> 00:17:00.652
This might actually work.

00:17:00.652 --> 00:17:02.521
Hormone from the umbilical cord.

00:17:02.521 --> 00:17:04.957
An enzyme from when
the body was a fetus.

00:17:04.957 --> 00:17:08.227
Well, the umbilical cord is
like a storehouse of bacteria.

00:17:08.227 --> 00:17:11.025
It might be able to hold off
the Raaja for a while.

00:17:29.515 --> 00:17:31.540
Huh? It just moved.

00:17:32.885 --> 00:17:34.820
Hey, Kaine.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.055
Can you hear me?

00:17:36.055 --> 00:17:40.559
Oh, come on, dear.
She's not even born yet.

00:17:40.559 --> 00:17:42.661
We figured out a name for her.

00:17:42.661 --> 00:17:45.186
We might as well start using it.

00:17:47.466 --> 00:17:49.802
This isn't Juna's.

00:17:49.802 --> 00:17:51.429
It's Kaine's.

00:17:54.907 --> 00:17:58.110
Kaine, come on out soon.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:17:59.445
Once you're born...

00:17:59.445 --> 00:18:03.779
...we'll go from just being
a couple to becoming a family.

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:10.522
It's warm.

00:18:10.522 --> 00:18:12.387
A warm light.

00:18:13.092 --> 00:18:16.858
A light I felt a long,
long time ago.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:20.163
Mom...

00:18:21.733 --> 00:18:24.600
What happened? What is this?

00:18:27.306 --> 00:18:32.835
This is the sound one hears
when still in the mother's womb.

00:18:33.378 --> 00:18:36.609
The memory of the fetus
in the sea of the womb.

00:18:43.388 --> 00:18:45.356
Detecting Earth Sympathy Reaction.

00:18:46.391 --> 00:18:49.995
No enemies, no friends...

00:18:49.995 --> 00:18:53.487
You tiny creatures
so bonded together...

00:18:53.966 --> 00:18:58.767
...come together and
now show that you are alive.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:11.917
The beneficial bacteria within
TI-2 is growing dramatically.

00:19:11.917 --> 00:19:14.386
It's growing at an
unbelievable rate!

00:19:14.386 --> 00:19:15.654
No way...

00:19:15.654 --> 00:19:18.757
Even with the umbilical cord,
how could it work so quickly?

00:19:18.757 --> 00:19:20.259
No.

00:19:20.259 --> 00:19:22.694
This is probably her brainwaves.

00:19:22.694 --> 00:19:24.889
No, her spirit.

00:19:32.704 --> 00:19:35.036
The Raaja responses
are disappearing.

00:19:35.707 --> 00:19:39.871
Her spirit moved the
lives of the small creatures.

00:19:57.963 --> 00:19:58.830
What?

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:00.766
TI-2 is doing something
very strange.

00:20:00.766 --> 00:20:01.698
What do you mean?

00:20:02.167 --> 00:20:03.327
Juna?

00:20:03.869 --> 00:20:05.131
What's going on?

00:20:05.804 --> 00:20:06.672
Tokio...

00:20:06.672 --> 00:20:07.764
Huh?

00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:16.143
The patient's brainwaves have
synchronized with that of TI-2.

00:20:16.848 --> 00:20:18.016
That's incredible.

00:20:18.016 --> 00:20:21.349
Even the intestinal bacteria
within the boy is growing.

00:20:40.606 --> 00:20:41.903
Chris...

00:20:43.542 --> 00:20:46.102
Juna... Juna...

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:15.941
Juna!

00:21:15.941 --> 00:21:18.739
You really worried me...

00:21:18.844 --> 00:21:19.708
Mom...

00:21:22.114 --> 00:21:24.383
Don't go anywhere anymore.

00:21:24.383 --> 00:21:25.680
I beg you.

00:21:27.152 --> 00:21:30.952
I'm sorry. I made you worry.

00:21:31.623 --> 00:21:32.724
Tokio?

00:21:32.724 --> 00:21:33.859
What about Tokio?

00:21:33.859 --> 00:21:36.795
They say Tokio's gotten over
the worst of it.

00:21:36.795 --> 00:21:38.430
There's nothing to worry about.

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:39.564
What?

00:21:39.564 --> 00:21:43.625
The doctor said that he'll be fine
once he rests up for a while.

00:21:44.403 --> 00:21:46.030
Thank goodness.

00:21:46.738 --> 00:21:50.697
And it was so nice of Sayuri
to stay here the whole time.

00:21:51.076 --> 00:21:54.443
That girl is so considerate.

00:21:56.214 --> 00:21:57.772
Sayuri...

00:21:59.685 --> 00:22:01.983
Juna? Are you all right?

00:22:03.288 --> 00:22:04.656
Mom, my stomach...

00:22:04.656 --> 00:22:06.385
Is it hurting again?

00:22:06.892 --> 00:22:08.587
I'm hungry.

00:22:09.294 --> 00:22:10.896
You just wait there.

00:22:10.896 --> 00:22:13.296
I'll make you some rice porridge.

00:22:13.598 --> 00:22:17.557
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:22:26.845 --> 00:22:33.518
Kinou no ame wa higashi
no machi ni

00:22:33.518 --> 00:22:38.353
Tsumetai hoshi wo furaseta

00:22:39.291 --> 00:22:46.064
Kanashi kimi wa hitori de
shizuka ni

00:22:46.064 --> 00:22:52.230
Atashi no daisuki na uta
wo kuchizusamu

00:22:53.972 --> 00:22:58.610
Ikanakucha fukai kurayami ni

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:01.680
Mayoikonda kare wo

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:05.741
Daremo tasukete kurenai

00:23:06.151 --> 00:23:11.022
Atashi nara itoshisa dake de

00:23:11.022 --> 00:23:14.059
Donna basho e demo

00:23:14.059 --> 00:23:18.497
Mayowanai de hashitte yukeru

00:23:18.497 --> 00:23:23.335
Dakara ooki na koe de

00:23:23.335 --> 00:23:31.470
Nandomo atashi no namae wo yonde

00:23:44.256 --> 00:23:48.625
Epilogue

00:23:50.896 --> 00:23:53.331
I wonder if human beings,
like the soil in a field...

00:23:53.331 --> 00:23:57.803
...don't get eaten up by bugs
or sick if they're healthy.

00:23:57.803 --> 00:23:59.504
It's not like that, Juna.

00:23:59.504 --> 00:24:00.672
Huh?

00:24:00.672 --> 00:24:01.973
I mean, look at it.

00:24:01.973 --> 00:24:05.568
Even the old man's garden
was full of bugs.

00:24:06.511 --> 00:24:08.308
Yeah, but...

00:24:08.847 --> 00:24:12.180
Yes, there are a lot.

00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:14.351
A lot of bugs.

00:24:14.653 --> 00:24:15.954
But...

00:24:15.954 --> 00:24:18.657
...because there are all kinds
of grasses and plants growing...

00:24:18.657 --> 00:24:21.091
...there're many different
kinds of bugs.

00:24:22.327 --> 00:24:24.729
If there are insects that
eat vegetables...

00:24:24.729 --> 00:24:27.562
...there are other insects
that eat those insects.

00:24:27.732 --> 00:24:31.269
And if there are insects that will
eat the remains of those insects...

00:24:31.269 --> 00:24:34.329
...there are other insects that
will bury the waste into the soil.

00:24:34.706 --> 00:24:35.941
So...

00:24:35.941 --> 00:24:38.410
...even if there are a lot of bugs...

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:40.344
...vegetables and rice can grow?

00:24:41.112 --> 00:24:43.181
Then, why?

00:24:43.181 --> 00:24:46.284
Why doesn't everybody
do like you do at your place?

00:24:46.284 --> 00:24:48.019
You don't have to till the soil...

00:24:48.019 --> 00:24:50.044
...and you don't have to
give it fertilizer.

00:24:50.455 --> 00:24:53.515
If you don't have to do anything
with it, it sure seems easier.

00:24:55.193 --> 00:24:57.559
You're right.

00:24:58.063 --> 00:25:00.832
But people have a hard time
getting out of a habit...

00:25:00.832 --> 00:25:02.663
...they're used to.

00:25:03.435 --> 00:25:05.971
People fear doing something
out of the ordinary...

00:25:05.971 --> 00:25:08.496
...and have it not turn out right.

00:25:09.541 --> 00:25:12.669
But the crops here
are turning out well.

00:25:13.411 --> 00:25:14.546
Well...

00:25:14.546 --> 00:25:17.849
...you can't say that you don't
have to do anything.

00:25:17.849 --> 00:25:20.418
When the rice plants and
vegetables are still young...

00:25:20.418 --> 00:25:25.423
...we need to take away the grasses
and weeds around them a little.

00:25:25.423 --> 00:25:28.960
Even when I started here,
everything would get...

00:25:28.960 --> 00:25:32.464
...eaten up by insects.
It was quite tough.

00:25:32.464 --> 00:25:33.498
Huh?

00:25:33.498 --> 00:25:35.090
Even at your place?

00:25:36.101 --> 00:25:38.763
The land has been
quite weakened.

00:25:39.571 --> 00:25:43.141
It might take a lot of years
before the grasses and the insects...

00:25:43.141 --> 00:25:46.076
...can make the soil healthy again.

00:25:46.845 --> 00:25:49.814
They make the
soil healthy themselves?

00:25:50.348 --> 00:25:52.009
They're so cute.

00:25:52.918 --> 00:25:54.286
Even in the same spot...

00:25:54.286 --> 00:25:58.189
...the weeds and grasses that grow
every year are of different types...

00:25:58.189 --> 00:26:01.560
...and the characteristics of
the soil change along with it.

00:26:01.560 --> 00:26:05.121
It gets soft and puffy.

00:26:06.865 --> 00:26:09.732
Puffy and warm...

00:26:10.068 --> 00:26:14.732
But who can wait years
for that to happen?

00:26:15.106 --> 00:26:18.076
On top of that,
all the vegetables here...

00:26:18.076 --> 00:26:21.046
...are of different shapes and sizes.

00:26:21.046 --> 00:26:25.574
You couldn't sell them at markets
or convenience stores.

00:26:25.984 --> 00:26:29.487
Oh, so they won't sell
in the end, huh?

00:26:29.487 --> 00:26:32.285
No wonder nobody
wants to go to the trouble.

00:26:34.192 --> 00:26:40.198
They're all different shapes
and sizes probably for a reason.

00:26:40.198 --> 00:26:41.967
Huh? Really?

00:26:41.967 --> 00:26:44.231
It's just the hobby of an old man.

00:26:44.869 --> 00:26:46.137
Even so...

00:26:46.137 --> 00:26:48.540
...this old man's hobby
can still...

00:26:48.540 --> 00:26:52.911
...easily come up with enough
food to feed ten or twenty people.

00:26:52.911 --> 00:26:54.779
Yeah, well.
That's not good enough.

00:26:54.779 --> 00:26:58.149
I mean, there're over
six billion people on Earth now.

00:26:58.149 --> 00:27:03.143
Being able to feed ten or twenty people
isn't even a drop in the bucket.

00:27:05.290 --> 00:27:06.814
It's true.

00:27:08.727 --> 00:27:11.252
That's just an old man's hobby.

00:27:11.963 --> 00:27:13.231
Hey, Tokio.

00:27:13.231 --> 00:27:14.493
Hm? What?

00:27:14.833 --> 00:27:16.835
Yeah, but...

00:27:16.835 --> 00:27:20.105
...that means if only one person
in ten does it as a hobby...

00:27:20.105 --> 00:27:22.972
...everybody can be fed, right?

00:27:25.377 --> 00:27:28.244
Only one in ten...?

00:27:30.215 --> 00:27:32.083
Episode 6:
The First One
